            "created_at": "2025-08-25T15:11:09.903229+00:00",
            "notes": "For round 2, we will take [Shieldbuster](item_9ee1f150-537d-40b9-b975-7820fb1c6a66) and [Aftermarket Firing Pin](item_2485b212-b286-42d0-a2bd-20eb4396b054). Both these abilities boost attack speed, [Shieldbuster](item_9ee1f150-537d-40b9-b975-7820fb1c6a66) is a staple of this build as it makes it very easy to 1v1 other tanks.\n\nWe will also be holding onto our Round 1 items, but if you can't afford it, I recommend selling [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf) rather than the other two green items we have, as the two rare items we just got already boost  [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed).\n\nOPTIONAL ITEMS FOR REST OF MATCH:\n\nIf you are facing a [Junker Queen](hero_4794d288-27d9-49e0-a1dd-ffe0f4de3ab1) or [Ana](hero_f1aee6cf-704f-455f-a100-ec882ebbe000), [Crusader\u2019s Cure](item_e89b853c-2441-432b-b4eb-20bc4b1b0619) can be a great choice to cleanse anti. This will be viable for the rest of the match, though I won't bring it up again in this guide. Remember though, this isn't necessary. Only go with this if you notice anti being an issue, and feel free to sell at any time.\n\nIf Sleep Darts from [Ana](hero_f1aee6cf-704f-455f-a100-ec882ebbe000) or Flashbangs from [Cassidy](hero_3dd63854-7558-4344-86e4-b506f807129b) are annoying you, [Cushioned Padding](item_20f2f4bc-4611-4d1f-b653-20f04d56b96f) is a good choice to mitigate their effects.\n\nAlso, if you can ever afford it, [Technoleech](item_cb7fd8bf-bdcc-439a-ad35-372f24a027a8) is a good option for the next few rounds for the bonus  [Weapon Lifesteal](stat_weapon_lifesteal).",
